  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 6 elbow routing depends on one-cell alignment: a downward stream aimed at an elbow's vertical stem can spill down its inner side as well as turn, while offsetting the elbow so the stream meets its horizontal arm can eliminate one leakage path and fill previously unreachable side sockets. Five ACTION5 commits on the same level ended the episode with GAME_OVER, confirming that commit attempts are a scarce resource independently of the longer whole-level action limit. Filling all four visible sockets was still insufficient while a stray stream remained, and a clean symmetric-offset candidate did not pass the fresh-reset gate, so at least one final routing or hidden condition remains unresolved.",
  "narrative": "Replayed the resolver's exact 278-action prefix from a fresh reset and confirmed levels_completed=5. On level 6, an initial spill mapped the two downward sources and the splitter/elbow behavior. The previously attractive non-crossing layout filled only the right and bottom sockets because the left elbow was flush against the vertical splitter; offsetting that elbow by one cell filled all four visible sockets, but the animation still showed an extra downward spill missing the bottom cup. A symmetric offset of the other elbow was attempted on the fifth commit, which ended the live episode before any level-up. I then compressed the hypothesized corrected layout to a 36-action one-commit suffix and ran reproduce() from a fresh reset; it reached only level 5, so no additional level is claimed. I stopped at 639 steps because the remaining 61-step budget cannot replay the 278-action prefix for another valid level-6 attempt or gate.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The resolver prefix is 278 actions and was directly confirmed from a fresh reset to reach levels_completed=5; any further reproduction gate needs at least those 278 calls.",
    "L6 directions are ACTION1=up, ACTION2=down, ACTION3=left, ACTION4=right; ACTION6 selects by rendered coordinate and ACTION5 commits.",
    "The vertical splitter cannot move left of x=14..16, so clearance from the left-turn elbow must be created by offsetting the elbow rather than moving the splitter toward the sockets.",
    "With the horizontal bar at x=23..37,y=20..22, place the left-turn elbow at x=20..25,y=29..34 rather than x=17..22: this changes the stream/elbow contact from the vertical stem to the horizontal arm and allows both left sockets to fill.",
    "The analogous clean candidate used the right-turn elbow at x=35..40,y=29..34, left-turn elbow at x=20..25,y=29..34, vertical splitter at x=14..16,y=26..37, and embedded-source horizontal bar at x=23..37,y=20..22; its one-commit fresh-reset gate still reached only level 5.",
    "The fifth ACTION5 commit on L6 returned GAME_OVER at levels_completed=5, so use failed commits sparingly even when the whole-level movement budget has not been exhausted."
